"Bosnia_and_Herzegovina": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Bosnia_and_Herzegovina-02166_-_Po%C4%8Ditelj_%2810476710854%29.jpg/1920px-Bosnia_and_Herzegovina-02166_-_Po%C4%8Ditelj_%2810476710854%29.jpg","title":"Bosnia and Herzegovina","desc":"The historic site of Počitelj is located on the river Neretva and it is south of Mostar. It is believed that the fortified town along with its settlements were built by Bosnia's King Stjepan Tvrtko I in 1383. The walled town of Počitelj evolved in the period from the 16th to the 18th centuries. Dennis G. Jarvis, CC BY-SA 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bosnia_and_Herzegovina-02166_-_Po%C4%8Ditelj_(10476710854).jpg","alt":"Bosnia and Herzegovina-02166 - Počitelj"},
