"Cowherd_and_Weaver_Girl": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Niulang_and_Zhinv_%28Long_Corridor%29.JPG/1920px-Niulang_and_Zhinv_%28Long_Corridor%29.JPG","title":"The meeting on the bridge of magpies","desc":"A painted panel in the Long Corridor of the Summer Palace in Beijing, which the file's own record identifies as the reunion of the Weaver Girl and the Cowherd on the bridge of magpies and dates to about the end of the 19th century. The painter is not named. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Niulang_and_Zhinv_(Long_Corridor).JPG","alt":"A wide painted panel on a wooden beam, framed by scrolling clouds. On the left a woman in green and blue robes strides forward with long yellow and blue ribbons streaming behind her; on the right a man in a broad conical hat turns towards her, and between them two small children reach out with their arms. Three magpies fly overhead."},
