"Naqada_culture": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Prehistoric_knife%2C_Naqada_II_period%2C_Egypt%2C_Petrie_Museum_UC_16294.jpg/1280px-Prehistoric_knife%2C_Naqada_II_period%2C_Egypt%2C_Petrie_Museum_UC_16294.jpg","title":"A ripple-flaked flint knife","desc":"A flint knife with a carved handle, photographed from both faces; the file's record identifies it as Naqada II and as Petrie Museum UC 16294, and credits the plate to a publication of 1896. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prehistoric_knife,_Naqada_II_period,_Egypt,_Petrie_Museum_UC_16294.jpg","alt":"A monochrome photograph, against a black ground, of a flint knife shown from both faces; one face of the broad blade is ground smooth and the other is covered in regular parallel flake scars, and the short handle is carved in low relief with rows of animals on one side and a serpent design on the other"},
"Narmer_Palette": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Narmer_Palette_smiting_side.jpg/1920px-Narmer_Palette_smiting_side.jpg","title":"Narmer Palette","desc":"The side of the Narmer Palette without the grinding hollow. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narmer_Palette_smiting_side.jpg","alt":"A shield-shaped greywacke slab carved in relief. Two cow-eared heads flank the top. Below, a large striding king in a tall white crown raises a mace over a kneeling captive he holds by the hair; a falcon perched on papyrus stems draws a rope through the lip of a human head. Two fallen figures lie at the foot."},
