"Pyramid_of_Djoser": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Saqqara_-_Pyramid_of_Djoser_complex_-_Heb-sed_Court_-_chapel.JPG/1920px-Saqqara_-_Pyramid_of_Djoser_complex_-_Heb-sed_Court_-_chapel.JPG","title":"A chapel in the heb-sed court of the Djoser complex","desc":"One of the chapels lining the heb-sed court inside the funerary enclosure at Saqqara, built of dressed limestone with a curved top and slender engaged columns. Daniel Mayer, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"Daniel Mayer, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons, https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saqqara_-_Pyramid_of_Djoser_complex_-_Heb-sed_Court_-_chapel.JPG","alt":"A tall limestone facade with a curved top and slender engaged columns, standing among low walls of dressed blocks in bright sunlight."},
