"Tomb_of_Aegisthus": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Inside_the_Tholos_Tomb_of_Aegisthus_%2815th_cent._B.C.%29_at_Mycenae_on_26_March_2019.jpg/1920px-Inside_the_Tholos_Tomb_of_Aegisthus_%2815th_cent._B.C.%29_at_Mycenae_on_26_March_2019.jpg","title":"Inside the Tomb of Aegisthus","desc":"The chamber of the tholos tomb at Mycenae known as the Tomb of Aegisthus, built of small stones; the beam and railing in the doorway are modern. George E. Koronaios, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inside_the_Tholos_Tomb_of_Aegisthus_(15th_cent._B.C.)_at_Mycenae_on_26_March_2019.jpg","alt":"The interior of a beehive tomb built of many small flat stones laid in courses, looking out through a doorway propped by a modern wooden beam."},
"Tomb_of_Clytemnestra": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/The_Tholos_Tomb_of_Clytemnestra_at_the_archaeological_site_of_Mycenae_on_26_March_2019.jpg/1920px-The_Tholos_Tomb_of_Clytemnestra_at_the_archaeological_site_of_Mycenae_on_26_March_2019.jpg","title":"The Tomb of Clytemnestra","desc":"The tholos tomb at Mycenae known as the Tomb of Clytemnestra, seen along its entrance passage; the triangular gap above the lintel relieves the weight upon it. George E. Koronaios, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Tholos_Tomb_of_Clytemnestra_at_the_archaeological_site_of_Mycenae_on_26_March_2019.jpg","alt":"A long passage walled with squared blocks running into a grassy hillside towards a tall doorway, with a triangular opening in the masonry above its lintel."},
"Tomb_of_the_Lions": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Inside_the_Tholos_Tomb_of_the_Lions_%2815th_cent._B.C.%29_at_Mycenae_on_26_March_2019.jpg/1920px-Inside_the_Tholos_Tomb_of_the_Lions_%2815th_cent._B.C.%29_at_Mycenae_on_26_March_2019.jpg","title":"Inside the Tomb of the Lions","desc":"The chamber of the tholos tomb at Mycenae known as the Tomb of the Lions, looking out through its doorway along the dromos. George E. Koronaios, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inside_the_Tholos_Tomb_of_the_Lions_(15th_cent._B.C.)_at_Mycenae_on_26_March_2019.jpg","alt":"The interior of a stone beehive tomb, looking out through a tall doorway spanned by a massive lintel into an open passage walled with squared blocks."},
