"The_Rape_of_the_Sabine_Women": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_The_Rape_of_the_Sabine_Women_-_WGA20310.jpg/1920px-Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_The_Rape_of_the_Sabine_Women_-_WGA20310.jpg","title":"Rubens, The Rape of the Sabine Women","desc":"Oil on oak, probably 1635–1640, National Gallery, London; Romulus watches from a throne at the right as the women are carried off.","credit":"Peter Paul Rubens, National Gallery, London (NG38), public domain, via Wikimedia Commons: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_The_Rape_of_the_Sabine_Women_-_WGA20310.jpg","alt":"A crowded Baroque painting: armoured men seize richly dressed women among columns and garlands, a robed figure enthroned on a dais at the upper right."},
