"Battle_of_Marathon": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Marathon_Tomb_of_the_Athenians_1.jpg/1280px-Marathon_Tomb_of_the_Athenians_1.jpg","title":"The Tomb of the Athenians at Marathon","desc":"The Soros, the burial mound raised on the plain of Marathon over the Athenians who fell in the battle. Pausanias saw slabs on it giving the names of the dead by tribe.","credit":"Photograph by Tomisti, via Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0). https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marathon_Tomb_of_the_Athenians_1.jpg","alt":"A large, smooth, dome-shaped mound of dry yellow grass rising from a flat field, framed by dark trees on either side under a clear blue sky."},
